{"chunk_id": "a6fb264ce576", "text": "As Rama prepares for his final departure from the world, he first gives eternal commands to his companions. Hanuman is told to remain on earth as long as Rama\u2019s story is told, while Jambavan is instructed to live until the beginning of the Kali Yuga. At dawn, Rama begins the Mahaprasthana\u2014the great final journey. Guided by the sage Vasishtha and preceded by sacred fires and rituals, he walks toward the Sarayu River in solemn silence. The procession becomes cosmic: Lakshmi walks at his side, his weapons assume human form, and the Vedas, sacred syllables, sages, and deities accompany him. Citizens, animals, monkeys, bears, and even invisible beings follow him in devotion. Ayodhya empties as all creation joyfully joins Rama\u2019s ascent toward heaven, turning his departure into a universal pilgrimage.\nRama begins his final Mahaprasthana, leading a vast, joyful procession of gods, sages, citizens, and creatures toward the Sarayu and heaven.\nThemes: divine departure, devotion of followers, cosmic procession, renunciation and transcendence, sacred ritual", "vector": [0.026530764997005463, -0.01423272117972374, -0.011702760122716427, 0.010424250736832619, -0.00820546131581068, 0.01164864283055067, -0.03190185874700546, -0.013333029113709927, -0.025164315477013588, -0.0006088141235522926, 0.00812428630888462, 0.01946852169930935, -0.003906557336449623, 0.01327891182154417, -0.002200186485424638, -0.0020141599234193563, 0.046378105878829956, -0.017615022137761116, 0.02995365485548973, 0.003451637690886855, -0.0019160732626914978, -0.011073651723563671, -0.0008646005881018937, -0.007650763727724552, -0.0037814120296388865, 0.005232418887317181, 0.01490918081253767, -0.030332472175359726, 0.010843656025826931, -0.011736582964658737, -0.008009287528693676, -0.0188461784273386, 0.002778559923171997, -0.010701599530875683, -0.020144982263445854, -0.000858681567478925, 0.008969861082732677, 0.009741025976836681, 0.0093689728528261